body:
## Observed defect

`buildBlockKit` cuts a valid supplementary Unicode character in half at its 3,000-unit section boundary, producing an unpaired high surrogate. This affects a long title or any generated section where an emoji/non-BMP character straddles the cut.

Reproduced on Node 24.19.0 against the **actual npm pm-slack-standup@2026.10.9 distribution** and independently against source commit **864e6da7383e854830b4914f0225a7ff4bc613df**. npm `gitHead` matches that commit; the downloaded tarball's SHA-512 matched registry integrity:
`sha512-X+zcKTFgspsxQAVOfSKWBrKy5I5UOFeFwQLwig/ekiN6BHOthC6C4U8XE6Sb0wXd20ccV+7QMef+ZlfCLDHYLA==`.

[Source truncator](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/blob/864e6da7383e854830b4914f0225a7ff4bc613df/index.ts#L1701-L1744)

## Sanitized reproduction

In a disposable directory, install `pm-slack-standup@2026.10.9` and `@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.12` from the official npm registry with lifecycle scripts disabled, then run this as an ES module:

```js
import assert from "node:assert/strict";
import { buildBlockKit } from "pm-slack-standup";

const opts = {
  format: "blockkit", includeDone: true, groupBy: "status",
  sections: ["in_progress"], mentionMap: {}, splitYesterday: false,
  sectionLabels: {}, upNextCount: Infinity
};
function render(title) {
  const data = {
    wip: [{ id: "pm-emoji", title, status: "in_progress" }],
    blocked: [], done: [], upNext: [], total: 1
  };
  return buildBlockKit(data, opts).blocks
    .find(block => block.type === "section").text.text;
}
const title = "a".repeat(2975) + "😀" + "b".repeat(100);
const output = render(title);
console.log({
  inputWellFormed: title.isWellFormed(),
  outputWellFormed: output.isWellFormed(),
  length: output.length,
  tail: JSON.stringify(output.slice(-8))
});
assert.equal(render("Short 😀 title").isWellFormed(), true);
assert.equal(render("a".repeat(3100)).isWellFormed(), true);
assert.equal(render("a".repeat(3100)).length, 3000);
assert.equal(output.isWellFormed(), true); // Fails today
```

Actual: input is well formed; output is not; length is 3000; tail contains `aaaaaa\ud83d…`.
Expected: clipping retains complete Unicode code points and stays within the existing size budget.

## Impact and limits

The renderer itself demonstrably corrupts valid Unicode before delivery. This may produce replacement characters or downstream interoperability problems. No Slack request was sent, and this report does **not** claim a verified Slack API rejection.

Short Unicode titles and long ASCII sections pass. The existing code-point-aware truncator in [pm-slack](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/blob/389ae059a6beea07e2d08e2daa3d97d9066102b5/index.ts#L1018-L1044) also preserves well-formedness for the equivalent boundary case.

## Ownership and prior decisions

Checked all 91 canonical PM item documents at the pinned tree, plus all-state GitHub issue/PR searches for surrogate, Unicode and truncation. No existing owner describes this defect.

The closed [Block Kit schema decision pm-slack-standup-rpty](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/blob/864e6da7383e854830b4914f0225a7ff4bc613df/.agents/pm/decisions/pm-slack-standup-rpty.toon) intentionally keeps one bounded section per bucket. Preserve that behavior. The closed [formatter test task pm-slack-standup-uf4j](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/blob/864e6da7383e854830b4914f0225a7ff4bc613df/.agents/pm/tasks/pm-slack-standup-uf4j.toon) covered validity/truncation but does not establish this Unicode boundary invariant.

## Acceptance criteria

- Clip only at a complete code-point boundary while retaining the current length ceiling and ellipsis policy
- Cover both ordinary and compact section rendering with non-BMP text at, before and after the clipping boundary
- Retain the short-Unicode and long-ASCII positive controls
- Run the regression against the built/packed public entry as well as source; do not require a Slack credential or live post
